{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014x8FxpvMaDQF4PDSKp1vdH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\timport { NextResponse } from \"next/server\";\n2\timport type { NextRequest } from \"next/server\";\n3\timport { ROOM_TYPES, PROPERTY } from \"@/data/rooms\";\n4\t\n5\t/**\n6\t * ARI (Availability, Rates, Inventory) endpoint for connectivity partners.\n7\t *\n8\t * Google Free Booking Links require a connectivity partner (e.g., Beds24,\n9\t * Cloudbeds, RoomRaccoon) to pull live rates and availability. This endpoint\n10\t * exposes the hostel's ARI data in a standard JSON format that partners can\n11\t * consume via their pull-based integration.\n12\t *\n13\t * Query params:\n14\t *   - checkin  (YYYY-MM-DD, required)\n15\t *   - checkout (YYYY-MM-DD, required)\n16\t *   - currency (default: MYR)\n17\t *\n18\t * Authentication: API key via x-api-key header (set ARI_API_KEY env var).\n19\t */\n20\texport function GET(request: NextRequest) {\n21\t  const apiKey = process.env.ARI_API_KEY;\n22\t  if (apiKey) {\n23\t    const provided = request.headers.get(\"x-api-key\");\n24\t    if (provided !== apiKey) {\n25\t      return NextResponse.json(\n26\t        { error: \"Unauthorized\" },\n27\t        { status: 401 },\n28\t      );\n29\t    }\n30\t  }\n31\t\n32\t  const params = request.nextUrl.searchParams;\n33\t  const checkin = params.get(\"checkin\");\n34\t  const checkout = params.get(\"checkout\");\n35\t  const currency = params.get(\"currency\") || \"MYR\";\n36\t\n37\t  if (!checkin || !checkout) {\n38\t    return NextResponse.json(\n39\t      { error: \"checkin and checkout query parameters are required (YYYY-MM-DD)\" },\n40\t      { status: 400 },\n41\t    );\n42\t  }\n43\t\n44\t  const checkinDate = new Date(checkin);\n45\t  const checkoutDate = new Date(checkout);\n46\t\n47\t  if (isNaN(checkinDate.getTime()) || isNaN(checkoutDate.getTime())) {\n48\t    return NextResponse.json(\n49\t      { error: \"Invalid date format. Use YYYY-MM-DD.\" },\n50\t      { status: 400 },\n51\t    );\n52\t  }\n53\t\n54\t  if (checkoutDate <= checkinDate) {\n55\t    return NextResponse.json(\n56\t      { error: \"checkout must be after checkin\" },\n57\t      { status: 400 },\n58\t    );\n59\t  }\n60\t\n61\t  const nights = Math.ceil(\n62\t    (checkoutDate.getTime() - checkinDate.getTime()) / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24),\n63\t  );\n64\t\n65\t  const rooms = ROOM_TYPES.map((room) => ({\n66\t    room_id: room.id,\n67\t    room_name: room.name,\n68\t    description: room.description,\n69\t    max_occupancy: room.maxOccupancy,\n70\t    total_inventory: room.totalUnits,\n71\t    available_units: room.totalUnits,\n72\t    rate: {\n73\t      nightly: room.nightlyRate,\n74\t      total: room.nightlyRate * nights,\n75\t      currency,\n76\t    },\n77\t    amenities: room.amenities,\n78\t  }));\n79\t\n80\t  const response = {\n81\t    property_id: PROPERTY.id,\n82\t    property_name: PROPERTY.name,\n83\t    checkin,\n84\t    checkout,\n85\t    nights,\n86\t    currency,\n87\t    timezone: PROPERTY.timezone,\n88\t    checkin_time: PROPERTY.checkinTime,\n89\t    checkout_time: PROPERTY.checkoutTime,\n90\t    rooms,\n91\t    booking_url: `https://pelangicapsulehostel.com/book?checkin=${checkin}&checkout=${checkout}`,\n92\t    updated_at: new Date().toISOString(),\n93\t  };\n94\t\n95\t  return NextResponse.json(response, {\n96\t    headers: {\n97\t      \"Cache-Control\": \"public, max-age=300, s-maxage=300\",\n98\t    },\n99\t  });\n100\t}\n101\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6d90c97-f395-42af-a0ca-354a9893adb6","uuid":"b477cdb8-c889-4ac3-a28f-93f896760443","timestamp":"2026-04-13T19:20:18.889Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\app\\api\\ari\\route.ts","content":"import { NextResponse } from \"next/server\";\nimport type { NextRequest } from \"next/server\";\nimport { ROOM_TYPES, PROPERTY } from \"@/data/rooms\";\n\n/**\n * ARI (Availability, Rates, Inventory) endpoint for connectivity partners.\n *\n * Google Free Booking Links require a connectivity partner (e.g., Beds24,\n * Cloudbeds, RoomRaccoon) to pull live rates and availability. This endpoint\n * exposes the hostel's ARI data in a standard JSON format that partners can\n * consume via their pull-based integration.\n *\n * Query params:\n *   - checkin  (YYYY-MM-DD, required)\n *   - checkout (YYYY-MM-DD, required)\n *   - currency (default: MYR)\n *\n * Authentication: API key via x-api-key header (set ARI_API_KEY env var).\n */\nexport function GET(request: NextRequest) {\n  const apiKey = process.env.ARI_API_KEY;\n  if (apiKey) {\n    const provided = request.headers.get(\"x-api-key\");\n    if (provided !== apiKey) {\n      return NextResponse.json(\n        { error: \"Unauthorized\" },\n        { status: 401 },\n      );\n    }\n  }\n\n  const params = request.nextUrl.searchParams;\n  const checkin = params.get(\"checkin\");\n  const checkout = params.get(\"checkout\");\n  const currency = params.get(\"currency\") || \"MYR\";\n\n  if (!checkin || !checkout) {\n    return NextResponse.json(\n      { error: \"checkin and checkout query parameters are required (YYYY-MM-DD)\" },\n      { status: 400 },\n    );\n  }\n\n  const checkinDate = new Date(checkin);\n  const checkoutDate = new Date(checkout);\n\n  if (isNaN(checkinDate.getTime()) || isNaN(checkoutDate.getTime())) {\n    return NextResponse.json(\n      { error: \"Invalid date format. Use YYYY-MM-DD.\" },\n      { status: 400 },\n    );\n  }\n\n  if (checkoutDate <= checkinDate) {\n    return NextResponse.json(\n      { error: \"checkout must be after checkin\" },\n      { status: 400 },\n    );\n  }\n\n  const nights = Math.ceil(\n    (checkoutDate.getTime() - checkinDate.getTime()) / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24),\n  );\n\n  const rooms = ROOM_TYPES.map((room) => ({\n    room_id: room.id,\n    room_name: room.name,\n    description: room.description,\n    max_occupancy: room.maxOccupancy,\n    total_inventory: room.totalUnits,\n    available_units: room.totalUnits,\n    rate: {\n      nightly: room.nightlyRate,\n      total: room.nightlyRate * nights,\n      currency,\n    },\n    amenities: room.amenities,\n  }));\n\n  const response = {\n    property_id: PROPERTY.id,\n    property_name: PROPERTY.name,\n    checkin,\n    checkout,\n    nights,\n    currency,\n    timezone: PROPERTY.timezone,\n    checkin_time: PROPERTY.checkinTime,\n    checkout_time: PROPERTY.checkoutTime,\n    rooms,\n    booking_url: `https://pelangicapsulehostel.com/book?checkin=${checkin}&checkout=${checkout}`,\n    updated_at: new Date().toISOString(),\n  };\n\n  return NextResponse.json(response, {\n    headers: {\n      \"Cache-Control\": \"public, max-age=300, s-maxage=300\",\n    },\n  });\n}\n","numLines":101,"startLine":1,"totalLines":101}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01VoSum1w9UinPA3eS7act5D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand better. There's already a basic ARI endpoint for US-194. However, US-196 requires:\n\n1. **Integration with a channel manager** (Beds24, Cloudbeds, or SiteMinder) - this means actually setting up an account and API keys\n2. **Two-way ARI sync** - not just read-only, but also push updates when bookings are made\n3. **Live availability from channel manager** - the current endpoint just returns all units as available\n4. **Zero overbookings** - needs validation\n5. **Google Hotel Center approved** - needs the channel manager to be an approved partner\n\nThis is a very large, complex task that requires:\n- Choosing a specific channel manager (the story doesn't specify which one)\n- Setting up accounts and getting API credentials\n- Creating client library code\n- Implementing webhook handling\n- Syncing with bookings\n- Real-time inventory management\n\nGiven that this is marked as \"large\" complexity and has already been attempted once without success, I think the realistic approach is to:\n\n1. Pick a channel manager (Beds24 seems like the popular choice for small hostels based on the progress.txt pre-analysis)\n2. Create the integration structure for it\n3. Document the setup requirements\n4. Create tests/documentation\n\nLet me think about what's the MINIMAL MVP that would satisfy the acceptance criteria:\n\n**Acceptance Criteria Analysis:**\n1. \"Channel manager account configured with Booking.com, Agoda, Hostelworld connections\" - This is MANUAL SETUP, not code\n2. \"Two-way ARI sync is live\" - This requires API integration + booking system modification\n3. \"Website availability calendar pulls live inventory\" - This requires modifying the ARI endpoint to pull from channel manager\n4. \"Zero overbooking incidents in 30-day period\" - This requires validation logic\n5. \"Channel manager is approved Google Hotel Center partner\" - This is about WHICH channel manager we choose\n\n\n6. Since this is a single story within one iteration and needs to stay under 350 lines, I should focus on the core integration: building a Beds24 API client, creating endpoints to fetch availability, implementing webhook handlers for updates, and modifying the booking system to sync with Beds24. The manual setup documentation can guide users through the rest.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2310,"cache_read_input_tokens":87244,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2310},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6d90c97-f395-42af-a0ca-354a9893adb6","uuid":"0858dc77-82c5-44b9-a9c6-8bc60be3ada9"}
