{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FZttKdtB4K3AnFAhvdXBkd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# SPIRAL Crash Report\n2\t# Story:     US-196\n3\t# Worker:    sequential\n4\t# Exit Code: 124\n5\t# Timestamp: 20260413T190359Z\n6\t# ─────────────────────────────────────────\n7\t\n8\tNo stderr capture available (exit_code=124)\n9\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6d90c97-f395-42af-a0ca-354a9893adb6","uuid":"3e1609c7-6243-4440-a670-547eed2c7cf5","timestamp":"2026-04-13T19:20:36.710Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\.spiral\\crashes\\US-196_20260413T190359Z.txt","content":"# SPIRAL Crash Report\n# Story:     US-196\n# Worker:    sequential\n# Exit Code: 124\n# Timestamp: 20260413T190359Z\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────\n\nNo stderr capture available (exit_code=124)\n","numLines":9,"startLine":1,"totalLines":9}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01AnxmdYYL2WPCVgCYD67Hfh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Exit code 124 is typically a timeout. So the previous attempt timed out trying to implement US-196. This story is genuinely very large.\n\nGiven the constraints:\n- This is a LARGE complexity story\n- It requires channel manager integration with real APIs\n- The previous attempt timed out\n- Must be < 350 lines added\n- This is meant to be completed in one iteration\n\nI think the realistic MVP for this story would be:\n1. Create a Beds24 API client library (since Beds24 is the recommended option for small hostels)\n2. Create environment configuration for Beds24 credentials\n3. Create webhook handler for incoming OTA updates\n4. Modify the ARI endpoint to fetch real data from Beds24 (instead of hardcoded inventory)\n5. Add booking sync logic to push bookings to Beds24\n6. Add TypeScript types and basic integration tests\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider. The story acceptance criteria say:\n- \"Channel manager account configured\" - this is manual setup\n- \"Two-way ARI sync is live\" - code requirement\n- \"Website availability pulls live inventory\" - code requirement\n- \"Zero overbooking incidents in 30-day period\" - operational requirement\n- \"Channel manager is approved Google Hotel Center partner\" - selection requirement\n\nThe key issue is: I need to actually SET UP a channel manager account with API credentials to implement this properly. Without that, I'm just writing code that won't be testable.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the story notes:\n- \"Recommended for small hostels: Beds24 (budget), Cloudbeds (mid-range), SiteMinder (enterprise)\"\n\nBut they DON'T require a specific choice in the story description. Let me think about what I CAN do:\n\n**Option 1: Implement with mock/stub channel manager**\n- Create the integration framework\n- Use mock data for testing\n- Documentation for real setup\n\n**Option 2: Focus on the architectural setup**\n\n\n- Build out the data structures and types needed\n- Create the API client skeleton with proper interfaces\n- Document the exact implementation steps for real credentials\n\nRe-reading the story more carefully, the goal is to have live OTA synchronisation. The acceptance criteria focus on: channel manager account configured with OTA connections, two-way ARI sync within 2 minutes, website calendar pulling live inventory, and zero overbooking. Since I can't set up real credentials, I should focus on building the framework that would support this once credentials are available.\n\nFor a more focused scope, I'll implement a minimal version using Beds24 as the OTA provider. This means building an API client to connect with Beds24, creating a webhook endpoint to receive availability updates, modifying the ARI endpoint to pull from the OTA's API, syncing new bookings back to the OTA, and adding inventory management to prevent overbooking.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":301,"cache_read_input_tokens":90470,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":301},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6d90c97-f395-42af-a0ca-354a9893adb6","uuid":"a9129571-3a34-4705-8f29-640454d4ba3c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01AnxmdYYL2WPCVgCYD67Hfh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis, US-196 is a **large, complex integration story** that requires real channel manager setup. The previous attempt timed out. I'll implement a minimal viable version focused on the critical code integration points:\n\n## Current State\n- Website has basic ARI endpoint from US-194 (hardcoded inventory)\n- Booking system is WhatsApp-based with no sync to external systems\n- No channel manager integration exists\n- No webhook handling for OTA updates\n\n## Problem Identified\nNeed to implement two-way synchronization with a channel manager (Beds24) so that:\n- Website bookings update OTA availability in real-time\n- OTA bookings update website inventory\n- Website availability shows live channel manager data\n\n## Planned Changes\n- Create `site/src/lib/beds24-client.ts` - Beds24 API client\n- Create `site/src/app/api/webhooks/beds24/route.ts` - Webhook handler for Beds24 events\n- Update `site/src/app/api/ari/route.ts` - Pull live availability from Beds24\n- Create `site/src/app/api/bookings/sync/route.ts` - Push bookings to Beds24\n- Create configuration file for Beds24 credentials\n- Add types and tests\n\n<plan>\n{\n  \"files_to_create\": [\n    \"site/src/lib/beds24-client.ts\",\n    \"site/src/app/api/webhooks/beds24/route.ts\",\n    \"site/src/app/api/bookings/sync/route.ts\",\n    \"site/src/lib/channel-manager-types.ts\",\n    \"site/src/config/channel-manager.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"files_to_modify\": [\n    \"site/src/app/api/ari/route.ts\",\n    \"site/.env.local.example\"\n  ],\n  \"functions_to_add\": [\n    \"Beds24Client.getAvailability\",\n    \"Beds24Client.syncBooking\",\n    \"Beds24Client.validateWebhook\",\n    \"handleBeds24Webhook\",\n    \"syncBookingToBeds24\"\n  ],\n  \"estimated_loc\": 280\n}\n</plan>\n\nNow implementing:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":n